  ---
  # 🛠️ Defect Detection Test – iOS App

  > **Detect structural defects in real-world surfaces — on-device, offline, instantly.**

  [![Platform](https://img.shields.io/badge/Platform-iOS%2016%2B-black?style=flat-square&logo=apple)](https://developer.apple.com)
  [![Model](https://img.shields.io/badge/Model-YOLOv8%20%2B%20CoreML-orange?style=flat-square)](https://ultralytics.com)
  [![UI](https://img.shields.io/badge/UI-SwiftUI-blue?style=flat-square&logo=swift)](https://developer.apple.com/xcode/swiftui)
  [![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-AGPL--3.0-red?style=flat-square)](https://ultralytics.com/license)

  ---

  ## What Is This?

  An iOS application that detects real-world structural defects — **cracks, mold, water damage, pipe leaks** — using a YOLOv8 model
  converted to CoreML and running entirely on-device.

  Pick a photo or use the camera. The model draws bounding boxes with class labels and confidence scores in real time. No network
  calls, no API keys, no cloud dependency.

  ---

  ## 🚀 Features

  | Feature | What It Does | Why It Matters |
  |---|---|---|
  | 🔍 **Real-Time Detection** | YOLOv8 via CoreML on every frame | Instant results with no latency |
  | 🖼️ **Camera + Gallery Input** | Live capture or photo library | Works in the field or from archived images |
  | 🏷️ **Bounding Boxes + Labels** | Overlays class name and confidence % | Shows exactly what was found and where |
  | 🔁 **Fallback Class Labels** | Hardcoded labels if model metadata is missing | Prevents crashes across model versions |
  | 🧠 **Fully On-Device** | CoreML inference — no server required | Works offline, no data leaves the device |
  | 📦 **Optimized .mlpackage** | Ships as `.mlpackage` for runtime | Faster startup, better memory management |

  ---

  ## ⚙️ Quick Setup (3 Steps)

  ### Step 1 — Clone the repository

  ```bash
  git clone https://github.com/your-username/defectdettest.git
  cd defectdettest

  Step 2 — Open the Xcode project

  open defectdettest.xcodeproj

  Step 3 — Build & Run

  Select a simulator or physical iPhone and press ⌘R.

  ▎ Tip: Use a physical device for real camera access and accurate inference speed — CoreML runs significantly faster on-device than
  ▎ in the simulator.

  ---
  🧪 Usage

  Launch the app
        │
        ▼
  Select or capture an image 📸
        │
        ▼
  CoreML runs YOLOv8 inference on-device
        │
        ├── Bounding box coordinates
        ├── Class label  (Crack / Mold / Water Damage / Pipe Leak…)
        └── Confidence score (0.0 – 1.0)
        │
        ▼
  BoundingBoxView overlays results on your image 🧠

  ---
  📂 Project Structure

  defectdettest/
  │
  ├── defectdettestApp.swift              # App entry point — SwiftUI lifecycle
  ├── ContentView.swift                   # UI logic for model selection and image prediction
  ├── BoundingBoxView.swift               # Draws bounding boxes + labels over image
  │
  ├── defect_detect.pt                    # YOLOv8 PyTorch weights (training artifact, not used at runtime)
  ├── DefectDetectionModel.mlmodel        # CoreML model — legacy format, kept for reference
  ├── defect_detect.mlpackage/            # Active model used at runtime (.mlpackage preferred)
  │
  ├── Assets.xcassets/                    # App icons and image assets
  ├── Item.swift                          # Data model helpers
  │
  ├── defectdettest.xcodeproj/            # Xcode project config
  ├── defectdettestTests/                 # Unit tests
  └── defectdettestUITests/               # UI automation tests

